      "young": 0.65,
      "sapling": 0.35,
      "_leaves": "The nature set (docs/art/nature; the look audit's fix plan 3): each role a list of models, any of them picked per tree (Quaternius Stylized Nature, Mac 2026-11-14, 'high quality like WC3': pine: Pine_1, 3, 4; oak: CommonTree_1-5; dead: DeadTree_1, 3, a share of the broadleaf woods' trees bare; bush: nt_bush; another model slots in by adding it to its list). Every model has its leaves in their own material (Leaves_*, Leaf_*: Quaternius; MI_Leaves: the Meshy set), which the season tints (terrain.gd's season pass; forest.gd _leaves names the leaves of a pine \"pine\", the rest \"leaves\"); the trunks keep their paint. seasons: by model file, a tint over its summer colour that replaces the season's own for that model, so a wood turns as a mix (art target 01-town: mostly deep green, some ochre and amber); a model not listed takes the season's tint for its kind. The leaves' colour (graded to deep green, its painted patchwork calmed) is the piece's own, made at import: data/meshy.json pieces.<name>.leaves.",
