      "_turn": "The leaves' turn by season and kind (forest.gd turn_of, terrain.gd's season pass): [r, g, b, amount], the colour mixed over the painted leaves through the material's detail layer and how much of it (g30 seasons: the old multiply alone left deep green leaves green in autumn). A model's own (seasons.<model>.turn) takes its place: CommonTree_1 amber, _3 ochre-olive, _5 russet, the rest the kind's own, so a wood turns as a mix. Pines and the evergreens have none. The season's multiply (terrain.gd SEASONS, seasons.<model>.<season>) still darkens or lightens under it.",
      "_evergreen": "Models outside the pine role whose leaves keep the pines' winter tint, not the broadleaves' turn (forest.gd leaf_kind; the towns' cypresses).",
