  "house_kit": {
    "_": "How house_tiers.gd composes a kit house of each tier from the Medieval Village kit (house_builder.gd bakes it; docs/TUNING.md). scale: the size a tiered kit house stands at, a share of the kit's metres (scale_kinds: the components it applies to; scale_tiers: the trades' tiers that stand at it too, one storey height round the square, their work spots scaled with them; mills keep the kit's, their sails and wheels hang in its metres): the kit's 3 m storeys and steep roofs stood a two-storey townhouse 9.7 m to the ridge and a merchant's 12-15 m beside 1.7 m townsfolk; at 0.85 a storey is 2.55 m, a townhouse 8.0-8.7 m to the ridge (research: a two-storey house 7-9 m), a three-storey merchant's or burgher's about 11.5. washes: the plaster's limewash colours (cream, white, ochre, rose, grey-blue, daub), a tint over the kit's plaster (above 1: the kit's plaster photo is a dull beige, so a warm cream wash lifts it; art target town-b: warm cream, ochre and rose plaster). stone_tint and timber_tint: the kit's stone (MI_UnevenBrick) and timber (MI_WoodTrim) on every kit house, lifted to honey stone and honey timber (they read near black under the grade). roof_weather: per house (by its seed) one of these multiplied over its roof covering's tint, new to dark weathered tile (house_tiers.gd _roof_look). stone_tint_v3: the tiered houses' stone under the v3 look, grey as 01-town's and the castle's (stone_tint, honey, otherwise); timber_tint_v3 their timber under v3, dark against white plaster (timber_tint otherwise). roof_uv: how many times more often the tile sheet repeats on a tiered roof (finer tiles; 1 the kit's). Round 3 (roofs huge, walls hidden): pitch lowered (tile 0.78, thatch 1.0, were 0.9, 1.12) and the square's tiers half-timbered more (townhouse, merchant, burgher timber 0.65, 0.6, 0.5). roof_tints: each roof covering's tint when team colour is off (team colour on draws thatch as straw and slate and shingle in these tones; look.json team.roofs). pitch: how steep each covering stands (a share of the kit's own pitch; thatch steepest). banner_scale: the holder's wall banner on a house's street front (extras.banner, Banner_1 is 1.6 x 2.4 m at 1). jetty_m: how far each upper storey of a jettied house leans out over the street (metres). Finesse (Mac 2026-11-12, 'no finesse'): window_glow, the kit's window glass as warm lit amber (colour, alpha, emission energy; house_builder.gd _glass); 01-town pass: the square's tiers thatched about 1 in 3, half-timbered over plaster (plain plaster 0.05), jettied more (townhouse 0.8, merchant 0.75, burgher 0.5); extras.door_lamp, a lantern on its post beside the front door (door_lamp: its file and height in metres; Kenney's town lantern, CC0); extras.door_frame, the kit's door frame round the front door (dark timber, stone on a stone front); shutters on most of the square's windows; a hanging sign on the forge, the armoury and the granary. tiers: per tier, ranges [lowest, highest] or numbers: w and d (2 m cells across the front and deep), floors, ridge (along: gable to the street, Manor Lords' burgage; across: eaves to the street with dormers, Anno's merchants), roofs and walls (weights: stone, stone_timber, timber, plaster), washes (which wash colours it may take), jetty (chance), dormers (per slope), dormers_back, chimney (chance of a stone stack up a gable), ridge_chimneys, pitch (on top of the covering's), round_windows (share), windows (share of wall panels with a window: front_ground, front, back, sides; party walls are mostly blind), shutters, shop (wide shop windows either side of the door), arcade (the ground floor's front open in arches), extras (chances; banner: the holder's banner down the upper street front; porch, sign, lean_to, outside_stair, balcony, window_boxes, vines), props (baked in: [piece, [x, y, z] metres, yaw, scale, anchor front|back|centre]; a bare name is the village kit's, res:// any glTF).",
